{"type":"record","name":"IbkrPreOpenManifest","namespace":"app.options.ibkr.gex","doc":"The armed strike universe for a trade date, under the reserved key __manifest|<tradeDate>. The browser materialises its skeleton rows from this and tears down any row absent from it, so the strikes array is the authoritative membership list. Published to options.ibkr.gex.status.v2 by databento-gex-service's pre-open IBKR GEX publisher (IbkrPreOpenService). The predecessor topic options.ibkr.gex.status carried hand-built JSON strings until 2026-10-17; this record reproduces that JSON FIELD FOR FIELD AND NAME FOR NAME. That is a hard requirement, not tidiness: the feed gateway converts these records to JSON for the browser with AvroJson, which emits exactly the published record's own fields, and option-chain.js reads them BY NAME. Renaming or retyping a field here changes what the browser receives. The registry subject is this record's FULL NAME, under RecordNameStrategy. That is deliberate and not the Confluent default, and here it is load-bearing rather than merely conventional: this ONE topic carries nine distinct value shapes, and a topic-name subject could not hold nine schemas. It also keeps one subject across environments, where TopicNameStrategy would mint a different subject per environment because the topic name carries the environment's TOPIC_PREFIX.","fields":[{"name":"manifestEpoch","type":"long","doc":"The generation this manifest was committed under."},{"name":"expectedCount","type":"int","doc":"How many strikes the manifest declares. Carried so a consumer can detect a truncated strikes array rather than silently treating it as a smaller universe."},{"name":"armSpot","type":"double","doc":"The canonical spot that priced the arm. A DOUBLE and not a decimal, deliberately: the predecessor JSON emitted this as a bare number from the same canonicalSpot value that the sibling GexStrikeAvro already carries as a double, and re-typing it here would change the number the browser renders. The price-as-decimal rule is about not introducing binary floating point for money, not about re-typing a faithful carry-over whose rendering is load-bearing."},{"name":"digest","type":"string","doc":"Digest over the manifest's conId map, so a consumer can tell two manifests apart without comparing every member."},{"name":"feedGeneration","type":"long","doc":"The feed generation adopted by the barrier when this manifest was committed."},{"name":"strikes","type":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"record","name":"IbkrPreOpenManifestStrike","doc":"One member of a pre-open manifest's strike universe. Nested inside IbkrPreOpenManifest and never published on its own.","fields":[{"name":"strike","type":"string","doc":"The strike as CANONICAL STRIKE TEXT, byte-identical to the form used in the record key ('7500', never '7500.0'). Deliberately a string and not a decimal: it is the key form, the browser coerces it with Number(), and a decimal logical type would reach the browser as a different rendering."},{"name":"callConId","type":"long","doc":"IBKR contract id of the call leg."},{"name":"putConId","type":"long","doc":"IBKR contract id of the put leg."}]}},"doc":"The strike universe, each with its call and put contract ids."}]}